      "worked_solution": "**Method 1** \n\nWe plot the given points in the coordinate plane.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14179134/assets/353bedad7a1692dea35f8b6adf30b7b461458c7852b4123a3fc865e1b23370a6.png)\n\nThe distance between two points is the length of the line segment that connects them.\n\nFrom the diagram, we see that the length of the segment is $7$ units, so the distance equals $7.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14179134/assets/e3516729d7662a3b4438a3d3085da3428605d026ba3387a71afeb085e2bd3e73.png)\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the distance between the two points by finding the distance of each point from the $x$-axis and then subtracting.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14179134/assets/f8c5583d14d4e5ca50df3ce906254446c402177734f352169d794de2bb7dea5c.png)\n\nThe point $(-5,-2)$ is at a distance of $2$ from the $x$-axis, and the point $(-5,-9)$ is at a distance of $9$ from the $x$-axis. Therefore, the distance between the two points is $9-2=7.$",
